<h2>Use Cases — From Content to Research</h2>
<p>The harness has such a wide range of uses that it would be a waste to use it only for development. These are cases the instructor built himself.</p>

<h3>Novel — "The Age of Agents"</h3>
<p>When he said "let's write an SF novel", the agents and skills for writing a novel got created.</p>
<ul>
    <li><strong>Character design agent</strong> &mdash; creating and developing the characters.</li>
    <li><strong>Worldbuilding agent</strong> &mdash; building the technology system and social structure of the setting (e.g. 2028&ndash;2032).</li>
    <li><strong>Science advisor agent</strong> &mdash; identifying and strengthening scientific errors · unrealistic elements in the manuscript.</li>
    <li>Brainstorming, science verification and the like were made into <strong>skills</strong> and injected into the agents.</li>
</ul>
<p>Flow: a one-line <strong>logline</strong> → the whole <strong>plot outline</strong> (a plan for tension and paying off foreshadowing chapter by chapter) → pre-generating the character · worldbuilding <strong>material</strong> → since the content of each chapter is already fixed, <strong>writing in parallel</strong> → science verification (e.g. correcting a random string into a string that is actually interpretable by a real algorithm and reflecting it).</p>

<h3>Webtoon</h3>
<p>When a webtoon was made from that same novel, a <strong>webtoon artist agent</strong> appeared, and a <strong>quality verification agent</strong> (checking character consistency · speech bubbles · errors) that catches odd panels was added. A <strong>loop</strong> was created to draw again when verification fails, so it ran through with a single "draw chapters 2 through 12".</p>

<h3>Other cases</h3>
<ul>
    <li><strong>Onboarding guide</strong> &mdash; researching and organizing what has happened since ChatGPT in December 2022.</li>
    <li><strong>Markdown viewer (mdview.kr)</strong> &mdash; first deployment in 40 minutes to an hour with a harness. Supports HWP import, and documents are <strong>stored only in the browser</strong> without being sent to a server.</li>
    <li><strong>Survey of the national AI data center</strong> &mdash; organizing the numbers and the timeline, plus critical/positive <strong>press analysis</strong> and the problems (business viability · GPU supply · power · data sovereignty). Because it is source-based, <strong>hallucination dropped sharply</strong>.</li>
    <li>Organizing things in <strong>newspaper style</strong>, planning research for an <strong>exam question service</strong>, and generating several <strong>UI templates</strong> to compare (planning with visible deliverables).</li>
</ul>

<div class="note">
    <span class="nh">What they have in common</span>
    Rather than "just write it", the <strong>agents · skills · workflow</strong> for doing that work are created first, and the result comes out on top of pre-planned material and a verification loop.
</div>
